      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6d558ff44e44ada717902|full_name}: I have no idea how to access to the log, will check it tonight.\nAbout a redoo step. \nOculus rift CV1 headset\nOS : Window 8.1\nRam : 8gb\nProcessor : i7 4790k 4Ghz\nGPU : 970 GTX (Last nvdia Driver)\n\nDefault oculus and default steam VR.\n\nStart oculus, start steam VR, launch VRchat. \nJoin any instance world. If the world is very very well optimized to run at 90fps on VR and almost nobody is in, it's most of time just fine.\n\nIf the world is unoptimized, supposed to run at 45 fps, or has a lot of people in (Which is the case of 90% of the worlds I do join when I play), the first time you'll join in, you'll have a 10-20 fps and bugged headtracking. You leave to home and come back and you'll get the smooth headtracking back and also the normal fps rate.\n\nIf you do open your steam vr, or oculus menu at any time in a 45 fps world, (And often in a 90 fps world too) and close the menu, you'll be lagging as hell forever at 20 fps with a bugged headtracking and will have to rejoin the world back again.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
